# Push completed work

After finishing a requested code change, commit it and push it to the current branch.

- Follow the repository git safety rules. Do not force-push, skip hooks, or change git config.
- Leave out secrets, `.env` files, and unrelated accidental edits.
- If the commit or push fails, fix the cause and try again with a new commit.
- Skip the commit only when the user says not to push, or when there is nothing to commit.
